IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`
IMPORT `er3-allocation`

-- Tests of er3-allocation (regulation 36). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of reg 36
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 608-667) before the module was run. Dates: 2026-03-04 is a Wednesday, so the Sunday
-- that begins its week is 2026-03-01; 2026-07-01 is a Wednesday, so its Sunday is 2026-06-28.

`test fact not earnings` MEANS `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35`
`test fact contract with services` MEANS `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services`
`test fact contract without services` MEANS `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment without the performance of services`
`test fact return to work` MEANS `er3 earnings: payable by an employer in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work`
`test fact self-employed` MEANS `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed`
`test fact commissions` MEANS `er3 earnings: from participation in profits or commissions`
`test fact from services` MEANS `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services`
`test fact from transaction` MEANS `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction`
`test fact farming` MEANS `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed in farming`
`test fact subsidy` MEANS `er3 earnings: received in the form of a subsidy`
`test fact vacation pay` MEANS `er3 earnings: vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation`
`test fact specific vacation` MEANS `er3 earnings: the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods`
`test fact lay-off` MEANS `er3 earnings: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`
`test fact award` MEANS `er3 earnings: paid or payable under a labour arbitration award or tribunal judgment, or as a settlement of an issue that might have been so determined`
`test fact award specific weeks` MEANS `er3 earnings: awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted`
`test fact pension moneys` MEANS `er3 earnings: the moneys referred to in paragraph 35(2)(e)`
`test fact periodic` MEANS `er3 earnings: paid or payable on a periodic basis`
`test fact lump sum` MEANS `er3 earnings: paid or payable in a lump sum`
`test fact holiday` MEANS `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day observed as such by law, custom or agreement`
`test fact holiday adjacent` MEANS `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day immediately preceding or following one that occurs at the establishment of the employer or former employer`
`test fact re-employment` MEANS `er3 earnings: payable under a government program intended to encourage re-employment, as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment`

GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
`test governing` facts MEANS `reg 36 the manner of allocation that governs` facts

§ `reg 36(20) -- rounding`

#ASSERT `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` 2.5 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` 2.49 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` 0.5 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` 0.49 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` 100 EQUALS 100

§ `reg 36(1), (2) -- what is allocated`

#ASSERT `reg 36(1) and (2) the earnings are allocated to weeks` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(1) and (2) the earnings are allocated to weeks` TRUE (LIST `test fact not earnings`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 36(1) and (2) the earnings are allocated to weeks` FALSE EMPTY EQUALS FALSE

§ `reg 36(3) -- a period that does not coincide with a week`

-- 2026-03-04 (Wednesday) to 2026-03-17 (Tuesday): 14 days, not a week.
`test period Wed to Tue` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 4), (YMD 2026 3 17)
-- 2026-03-01 (Sunday) to 2026-03-07 (Saturday): exactly a week.
`test period exactly a week` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 7)

#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the period does not coincide with a week` `test period Wed to Tue` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the period does not coincide with a week` `test period exactly a week` EQUALS FALSE
-- Sunday 03-01 holds Mar 4-7 of the period; 03-08 is wholly in; 03-15 holds Mar 15-17; 03-22 and 02-22 are outside.
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 8) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 22) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 2 22) EQUALS FALSE
-- 1000 payable, 10 days worked in the period: 3 in the first week, 5 in the second, 2 in the third.
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) 3 10 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 8) 5 10 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 15) 2 10 EQUALS JUST 200
-- a week outside the period gets none of it.
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 22) 0 10 EQUALS JUST 0
-- rounding by (20): 700 x 3/9 = 233.33 is 233; 1000 x 2/3 = 666.67 is 667; 5 x 1/2 = 2.5 is 3.
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 700 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) 3 9 EQUALS JUST 233
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2 3 EQUALS JUST 667
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 5 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) 1 2 EQUALS JUST 3
-- not covered by (3): the period is a week; no day was worked in the period.
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period exactly a week` (YMD 2026 3 1) 5 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` 1000 `test period Wed to Tue` (YMD 2026 3 1) 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `reg 36(4) to (7) -- the manner for earnings from services, transactions and profits`

#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact contract with services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact contract without services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact return to work`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact commissions`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact from transaction`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact commissions`, `test fact from transaction`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned`
-- (6.2) does not apply when the earnings arise from services.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.2) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from neither services nor a transaction` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7) farming: a transaction goes by (6.1), a subsidy to the week it was paid, services by (6).
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact farming`, `test fact from transaction`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact farming`, `test fact subsidy`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the subsidy was paid`
#ASSERT `reg 36(7) earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact farming`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact self-employed`, `test fact farming`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`
-- a subsidy to someone who is not farming: (7) does not apply.
#ASSERT `reg 36(7) earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming` (LIST `test fact subsidy`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the week of a subsidy paid Wednesday 2026-03-04 is the week of Sunday 2026-03-01.
#ASSERT `reg 36(7)(b) the week to which a farming subsidy is allocated` (YMD 2026 3 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1

§ `reg 36(6.1), (6.2) -- transactions and equal shares`

-- The maximum yearly insurable earnings is taken as 52000 so that the weekly threshold is exactly 1000.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1)(a) the aggregate is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52` 1001 52000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1)(a) the aggregate is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52` 1000 52000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1)(a) the aggregate is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52` 999 52000 EQUALS FALSE
-- (a): over the threshold, to the weeks of the work, or to the week of the transaction if no work was done.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` 2000 52000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` 2000 52000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er3 transaction: to the week in which the transaction occurred`
-- (b): at or under the threshold, to the week of the transaction, or to the weeks of the work if the claimant demonstrates the work was in more than one week.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` 1000 52000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er3 transaction: to the week in which the transaction occurred`
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` 1000 52000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` 1000 52000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
-- the share of 3000 for a week with 2 of 6 units of work is 1000; 1000 x 1/3 is 333; no work at all is not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) the share of the earnings allocated to a week in proportion to the work` 3000 2 6 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) the share of the earnings allocated to a week in proportion to the work` 1000 1 3 EQUALS JUST 333
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.1) the share of the earnings allocated to a week in proportion to the work` 1000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6.2): 1000 over 4 weeks is 250 a week; over 3 weeks 333; no week is not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.2) the equal share allocated to each week` 1000 4 EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.2) the equal share allocated to each week` 1000 3 EQUALS JUST 333
#ASSERT `reg 36(6.2) the equal share allocated to each week` 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `reg 36(8) -- vacation pay`

#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact vacation pay`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: vacation pay in any other case, at normal weekly earnings for each week but the last`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact vacation pay`, `test fact specific vacation`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: vacation pay for a specific vacation period, made up to normal weekly earnings`
-- vacation pay by reason of a lay-off is (9)'s, not (8)'s.
#ASSERT `reg 36(8) vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation` (LIST `test fact lay-off`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8)(b): 1000 at normal weekly earnings of 400 is 400, 400 and the last week 200.
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` 1000 400 EQUALS LIST 400, 400, 200
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` 800 400 EQUALS LIST 400, 400
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` 1000.5 400 EQUALS LIST 400, 400, 201
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` 0 400 EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` 1000 0 EQUALS EMPTY
-- (8)(a): 1000 over a vacation of three weeks with 0, 100 and 0 of other earnings from the employment on them:
-- 400 (400 less 0), 300 (400 less 100) and 300 (what is left), all of it fitting in the three weeks.
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` 1000 400 (LIST 0, 100, 0) EQUALS LIST 400, 300, 300
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(a) the vacation pay that does not fit on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` 1000 400 (LIST 0, 100, 0) EQUALS 0
-- 1500 does not fit: 400, 300 and 400 are put on the three weeks, and 400 is left over (fork F5).
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` 1500 400 (LIST 0, 100, 0) EQUALS LIST 400, 300, 400
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(a) the vacation pay that does not fit on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` 1500 400 (LIST 0, 100, 0) EQUALS 400
-- 500 is used up in two weeks: 400 and 100.
#ASSERT `reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` 500 400 (LIST 0, 100, 0) EQUALS LIST 400, 100

§ `reg 36(9) to (11) -- lay-off or separation, and awards`

#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact lay-off`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: earnings by reason of a lay-off or separation, at normal weekly earnings from the week of the lay-off or separation`
-- (9): 3500 at normal weekly earnings of 1000, with 0 and 200 of other earnings from the employment on the first two weeks:
-- 1000, 800 (1000 less 200), then 1000, then the last 700.
#ASSERT `reg 36(9) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` 3500 1000 (LIST 0, 200) EQUALS LIST 1000, 800, 1000, 700
#ASSERT `reg 36(9) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` 3000 1000 EMPTY EQUALS LIST 1000, 1000, 1000
-- (10): 3500 allocated, 500 more arrives: the total of 4000 is allocated again.
#ASSERT `reg 36(10) the revised amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` 3500 500 1000 EMPTY EQUALS LIST 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000
-- (11): both facts needed; 2500 at 1000 a week is 1000, 1000 and 500.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact award`, `test fact award specific weeks`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: an award or settlement for specific weeks, at normal weekly earnings from the first week awarded`
#ASSERT `reg 36(11) earnings awarded for specific weeks following a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted` (LIST `test fact award`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 36(11) earnings awarded for specific weeks following a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted` (LIST `test fact award specific weeks`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 36(11) the amounts put on the consecutive weeks beginning with the first week awarded` 2500 1000 EMPTY EQUALS LIST 1000, 1000, 500

§ `reg 36(10.1), (10.2) -- when the lay-off allocation does not apply`

-- A base case in which every condition holds; each assertion changes what its comment says.
-- Allocation period 2009-06-07 to 2009-07-04 (28 days, four weeks), notified 2009-06-10, lay-off earnings 6000
-- (80% of which is 4800).
GIVEN bp IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
      weeks IS A NUMBER
      notified IS A DATE
      referral IS A DATE
      full IS A BOOLEAN
      courseWeeks IS A NUMBER
      cost IS A NUMBER
      entire IS A BOOLEAN
      begins IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test 10.1 case` bp years weeks notified referral full courseWeeks cost entire begins MEANS
    `reg 36(10.1) the allocation under subsection (9) does not apply` bp years weeks (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 6 7), (YMD 2009 7 4)) notified referral full courseWeeks cost 6000 entire begins

#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- (a) the benefit period begins January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010, both ends included.
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 1 25) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 1 24) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2010 5 29) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2010 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2010 5 30) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2010 6 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) at least seven of the 10 years; (c) fewer than 36 weeks.
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 6 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 10 36 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 10 0 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- (d) the referral: during the allocation period (4 weeks, so five or fewer), or within six weeks after notification (2009-06-10 + 42 days = 2009-07-22).
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 10) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 22) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 23) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 1) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- a six-week allocation (42 days) is not "five weeks or less": only a referral during the period counts.
#ASSERT `reg 36(10.1)(d) the referral is within the window of the allocation` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 6 7), (YMD 2009 7 18)) (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 25) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 36(10.1)(d) the referral is within the window of the allocation` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 6 7), (YMD 2009 7 18)) (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 18) EQUALS TRUE
-- exactly five weeks (35 days) is "five weeks or less".
#ASSERT `reg 36(10.1)(d) the referral is within the window of the allocation` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 6 7), (YMD 2009 7 11)) (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 7 20) EQUALS TRUE
-- (d)(i) full-time; (ii) 10 weeks, $5,000 or 80% of 6000 (4800); (iii) the whole cost; (iv) begins in the 52 weeks after the benefit period begins (2009-06-07).
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) FALSE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 9 4000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 10 4000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 9 5000 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 9 4800 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 9 4799 TRUE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 FALSE (YMD 2009 9 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2009 6 8) EQUALS TRUE
-- 2009-06-07 plus 364 days is 2010-06-06.
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2010 6 6) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `test 10.1 case` (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 35 (YMD 2009 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 20) TRUE 12 3000 TRUE (YMD 2010 6 7) EQUALS FALSE
-- (10.2): the allocation is made again under (9) if a ground for ending the referral exists.
#ASSERT `reg 36(9) the earnings are allocated under subsection (9), after subsections (10.1) and (10.2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 36(9) the earnings are allocated under subsection (9), after subsections (10.1) and (10.2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 36(9) the earnings are allocated under subsection (9), after subsections (10.1) and (10.2)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `reg 36(12) to (19) -- the remaining kinds of earnings`

-- (12): each of the seven kinds goes to the weeks in respect of which it is paid or payable.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment referred to in paragraph 35(2)(d) or (f)`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a family member`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
-- (13): a holiday or non-working day, or one next to one at the employer's establishment.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact holiday`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the holiday or non-working day occurs`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact holiday adjacent`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the holiday or non-working day occurs`
-- Wednesday 2026-07-01: the week of Sunday 2026-06-28.
#ASSERT `reg 36(13) the week to which a payment for a holiday or non-working day is allocated` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 28
-- (14) and (15): pension moneys by whether periodic or a lump sum.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact periodic`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: periodic pension moneys, to the period for which they are paid or payable`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact lump sum`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: lump-sum pension moneys, at the weekly annuity amount from the first week`
-- the periodic fact alone, without the pension moneys, is not (14).
#ASSERT `reg 36(14) pension moneys paid or payable on a periodic basis` (LIST `test fact periodic`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 36(15) pension moneys paid or payable in a lump sum` (LIST `test fact lump sum`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (15): a lump sum of 600 at a weekly amount of 250: 250, 250, then the last week 100.
#ASSERT `reg 36(15) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week the lump sum is paid or payable` 600 250 EQUALS LIST 250, 250, 100
-- (16): of the earnings already on a week, those allocated under (14) or (15) are left out: 300 + 100.
#ASSERT `reg 36(16) the earnings taken into account in allocating other earnings` (LIST (`er3 Earnings already on a week` OF 300, FALSE), (`er3 Earnings already on a week` OF 200, TRUE), (`er3 Earnings already on a week` OF 100, FALSE)) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `reg 36(16) the earnings taken into account in allocating other earnings` EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- (17): B = [sum of tPx/(1+i)^t - 0.5] x 52. One term of 1: (1 - 0.5) x 52 = 26. Two terms of 1 at i = 0: (2 - 0.5) x 52 = 78.
-- Terms 1 and 0.5 at i = 25%: 1 + 0.5/1.25 = 1.4, so (1.4 - 0.5) x 52 = 46.8.
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) B, the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime` (LIST 1) 0 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) B, the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime` (LIST 1, 1) 0 EQUALS 78
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) B, the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime` (LIST 1, 0.5) 0.25 EQUALS 46.8
-- i is rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage: 3.45% is 3.5% (the half goes up); 3.44% is 3.4%; 25.04% is 25%.
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) the yield i rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage` 0.0345 EQUALS 0.035
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) the yield i rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage` 0.0344 EQUALS 0.034
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) B, the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime` (LIST 1, 0.5) 0.2504 EQUALS 46.8
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) one plus the yield to the power of the number of years` 1.25 2 EQUALS 1.5625
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) one plus the yield to the power of the number of years` 1.25 0 EQUALS 1
-- A / B: 7800 / 78 = 100; B not above zero is not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) the weekly amount A / B` 7800 78 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `reg 36(17) the weekly amount A / B` 7800 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (18)
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact re-employment`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`

§ `reg 36(19) and the whole section`

-- (19)(a), (b): earnings to which none of (1) to (18) applies.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact from services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact from transaction`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the transaction occurs`
-- (19) does not apply when an earlier subsection does: services under a contract give only (4).
#ASSERT `reg 36 the manners of allocation that apply` (LIST `test fact contract with services`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS LIST `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
-- earnings that arise from neither services nor a transaction and are in no other subsection: not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 36(19) earnings to which none of subsections (1) to (18) apply` EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `test governing` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- Wednesday 2026-03-04: the week of Sunday 2026-03-01.
#ASSERT `reg 36(19)(b) the week to which earnings from a transaction are allocated` (YMD 2026 3 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- (2) is asked first: earnings that were never earnings are not allocated, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `test governing` (LIST `test fact not earnings`, `test fact contract with services`) EQUALS JUST `er3 manner: not allocated to any week`
-- Where two subsections apply the encoding lists both, in its own order (fork F3): a commission earner under a contract of employment.
#ASSERT `reg 36 the manners of allocation that apply` (LIST `test fact contract with services`, `test fact commissions`, `test fact from services`) EQUALS LIST `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`, `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
